      "answer": "Southwest Airlines, American Airlines, and United Airlines are identified as the primary US operators of Boeing 737 MAX aircraft, and compliance with the MCAS-related ADs is mandatory for all Part 121 operators. The FAA ADs apply to all Boeing Model 737-8 and 737-9 airplanes certificated in any category.",
