      "retrieval_mode": "full_context",
      "routing_reason": "full_context_profile",
      "n_contexts": 12,
      "answer": "The 2022 directive (FAA AD 2022-03-07) supersedes the 2020 directive (FAA AD 2020-05-11), and is itself superseded by the 2024 directive (FAA AD 2024-01-02). The 2024 AD's references state that AD 2020-05-11 was \"partially superseded by AD 2022-03-07, fully superseded by this AD.\"\n\nFor current operators: the 2024 directive is the one in force. It requires MCAS Software v2.0 or later to be installed within 90 days after its effective date (February 15, 2024), and states that 737-8/737-9 aircraft must not be operated with MCAS Software v1.7.3 or earlier after the compliance date. Operators still on v1.7.3 (e.g., Southwest's 87 aircraft and G-ABCD, both shown with a May 15, 2024 deadline) must complete the v2.0 installation by that date.",
      "citations": [
        "FAA-AD-2020-05-11",
        "FAA-AD-2022-03-07",
        "FAA-AD-2024-01-02"
      ],
      "error": null
